<title>ITALY: BankNapoli stock rises after rescue vote.</title>
<headline>BankNapoli stock rises after rescue vote.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco di Napoli savings shares rose sharply on the Milan stock exchange after the Italian government won a confidence vote in the Senate upper house to convert into law a decree covering a rescue plan for the troubled southern bank.</p>
<p>&quot;There is some buying interest for the stock even if volumes, although a bit up on the recent daily average, are still fairly low,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>At 1345 GMT, Banco di Napoli's savings share, the only one quoted, was up 5.6 percent at a session high of 570 lire in volume of just over 200,000 shares. The all-share Mibtel index was up just 0.62 percent.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
